# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the Swift drafter window (tp4/swift-drafter; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/swift-drafter and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# TWO IMAGES FROM ONE COMMIT: tp4-swift-drafter-0 (the control: the served drafter, manifest dedf8df6) and tp4-swift-drafter-1 (the candidate: the served drafter fine-tuned on Swift-1.5's own greedy text,
# manifest sw1-ft1-f8013036). Both tags are PLACEHOLDERS for the tags B0 and B1 build from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-swift-drafter-0/<tag>/;s/tp4-swift-drafter-1/<tag>/' *.env);
# a build skips a tag that already exists, so the tags must be fresh, and a commit of a file an image carries needs a new B0 and B1. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): Swift-1.5, the checkpoint the cards serve; BOTH images serve it with its own converted-weight directory. The drafter is the only difference.
# T1 (the CONTROL arm of the pair): the W-T1 tau lab (c2_tau_lab.py) on Swift-1.5 with the SERVED drafter (drafter arm 'control', image tp4-swift-drafter-0): Swift's own greedy answers to coding-agent turns, thinking ON,
# the arms A1 (public coding-agent turns) and A2 (the scrubbed own-session set). A3 is left out on purpose: it is the calibration of the BASE model's stack against a reference made on the base, so
# a Swift run may fail it by construction and the lab would stop. The profile is c2-packed-tp4 (the drafter proposes 15 tokens per round). The lab refuses the arm, before anything is sent, unless the
# container's log shows the Swift checkpoint lines. READ: "[TAULAB-REPORT] ... complete=True". NOTE THE RUN ID of this job: T2 pairs with it (C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL). Duration (estimate): 75 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-swift-drafter-0
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=control
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A1 A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=70
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=8
